# Verify map

How `/verify`, `/test` and `/ship` check each surface. Delete each example row once you add real ones.

## Where a local run lands

`LOCAL_RUN` in `CLAUDE.md` is the one home of this fact (`isolated` or `production`). Here, give the evidence. Example
only: `.env` points at the one production database and the live provider accounts, so a local run is a production
run.

With `LOCAL_RUN` = `production`, a local check is allowed only from the safe list below. Every other surface is
checked **after merge**, from the logs and a read-only query, never by running it locally.

## Safe to run locally

An action goes on this list only when its code path is read and nothing on it reaches the outside world: no database
write (except rows carrying the synthetic marker), no external call, no message, email or alert sent, no token
refreshed, rotated or saved, no job started, enqueued or drained. Follow every call: dynamic imports, queue
handlers, and what a job does when it finds real work waiting. A flag named `--dry-run` is a claim, not a fact, and
it covers only the entry point it was read in. A job with no dry-run flag is not on this list.

| Action | What it shows | Checked side-effect free (file:line) |
|---|---|---|
| `scripts/send-reminders --dry-run` | Example only: the reminders it would send | Example only: `scripts/send-reminders.mjs:40` returns before the send and the DB update |

## Changed path → how it is verified

`Local check` names a row of the safe list, or `none`. `none` means `/verify` gives `DEFERRED`, and the
after-merge check is the proof.

| Changed path | Local check | After-merge check | Evidence to capture |
|---|---|---|---|
| `server/routes/invoices/**` | Example only: dev server, call the route with a test session | Example only: the route's log line | Example only: response body + log line |
| `worker/jobs/**` | Example only: none | Example only: the job's next run in the logs, then a read-only count query | Example only: log line + query result |

## Irreversible side effects (never run as a test)

| Action | Why | Safe alternative |
|---|---|---|
| Charging a card | Example only: real money moves | Use the provider's test mode |

## Protected fixtures and seeds

| Fixture or seed command | Rule |
|---|---|
| `npm run seed:demo` | Example only: safe to re-run; never edit the protected demo account |

## Test accounts

Env var names only, never values or passwords.

| Env var | Holds |
|---|---|
| `TEST_USER_EMAIL` | Example only: login for the standard test user |
